  "_doc": "F-033: native Zig math builtins vs the compiled script. Every `expect` here is the verdict of the TS-compiled script on @bsv/sdk Spend.validate (asserted by packages/runar-testing/src/__tests__/f033-zig-native-math-onchain.test.ts); packages/runar-zig/src/builtins_math_onchain_test.zig asserts the native Zig runtime returns the same value. `expect: \"abort\"` means the script fails (the native runtime must abort, which examples/zig covers through assert_probe). Integers only; all values in `cases` fit i64. `wideCases` (N-030) holds vectors whose operands or results do NOT fit i64 (log2 exact past 2^64 since N-103, gcd stopping after 256 Euclid steps, sqrt's 2^495 guard, ...); every integer there is a DECIMAL STRING so no JSON reader rounds it, and it is executed on Spend by the same test. N-030: this one file drives every native runtime and every SDK ANF interpreter in all 7 tiers (the n030 math-builtins vector tests in runar-lang, runar-sdk, runar-go, runar-rs, runar-py, runar-rb, runar-zig, runar-java); i64-only components replay `cases` only.",
